  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The new Input 2.0 allows for a much more versatile range of binding configurations, however, one thing that effects my accessibility to the game has been removed from Input 2.0; the ability to open the Right Hand Quick Menu with my Left Controller, or vice versa.\n\n    The new bindings are simply \"Menu\", \"Quick Menu\", and \"Action Menu\". A logical decision for the sake of simplicity. But, as a result, the behavior follows which ever 'Handed controller' the binding is used on. This is not very accessible. In prior versions, I had used the separate Left/Right Hand Menu bindings to open the Right Hand Quick Menu on my Left Controller. Due to a physical disability I have in my Right Hand (Cerebral Palsy), I cannot use my Right Hand very well, so placing the Right Hand Quick Menu binding on my Left Controller was my best bet while keeping Two-Handed play. As it is, I can no longer access my Quick Menu the way I NEED to. Especially for important 'Here' tab actions like viewing the instance player list or rejoining the instance.\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this!",
